# Put the interfaces in their zones (this changes traffic at once):
#   zone DMZ / interface vlan20-dmz
#   zone LAN / interface bridge-lan
#   zone GUEST / interface vlan30-guest
#   zone WAN / interface ether1
# Written inactive:
#   defconf: accept in ipsec policy: not converted: ipsec-policy=in,ipsec (traffic of IPsec tunnels)
#   banned scanners: not converted: address list 'scanners', which rules fill while the router runs
#   old partner access: every service but some: a service object of ZLD lists what it matches
#   nothing but TCP: every service but some: a service object of ZLD lists what it matches
#   nothing but TCP-2: every service but some: a service object of ZLD lists what it matches
#   rest of the DMZ: not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish web' (203.0.113.3, 172.16.20.10); not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish mail' (203.0.113.4, 172.16.20.11)
#   rest of the DMZ-2: not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish web' (203.0.113.3, 172.16.20.10); not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish mail' (203.0.113.4, 172.16.20.11); every service bu
#   rest of the DMZ-3: not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish web' (203.0.113.3, 172.16.20.10); not converted: negated destination that does not name the same on both sides of NAT rule 'publish mail' (203.0.113.4, 172.16.20.11)
#   LAN to the package mirrors: 'mirrors' holds members only its platform knows
#   office hours for staff: schedule 'time=8h-18h,mon,tue,wed,thu,fri' is not converted; the rule would apply at all times
